      "A": "Research multicore execution while retaining the original arithmetic. Partition target bodies i into contiguous, balanced ranges across at most four CPU workers; each worker computes complete ascending-j sums and exclusively updates its targets' velocities. Use a persistent team across all ten iterations, with barriers before position integration and before the next force sweep. Avoid inner-loop reductions, atomics and dynamic scheduling. Use only threading facilities supported by the unchanged build; do not assume OpenMP is enabled or change compiler options. Within the existing budget, compare serial and four-worker execution, examining intermediate worker counts or a general small-n serial cutoff only when useful. Deliver a complete validated candidate and end-to-end measurements including thread startup.",
      "B": "Research exact SIMD and data layout, initially independently of threading. Compare the original layout with structure-of-arrays working storage, preserving the original binary layout at input/output boundaries. Vectorize across target bodies, broadcasting each source j and retaining separate, ascending-j accumulators in every lane; do not horizontally reduce the source dimension. Explore modest target register blocks using ARM64 SIMD supported by the fixed target, without assuming SVE. Preserve float intermediates, widen squared distances to double for square root and reciprocal division, then narrow inv_dist to float before the original float products. Do not substitute sqrtf, reciprocal-square-root estimates or reassociated sums. Match reference contraction behavior and handle arbitrary tails safely. Measure conversion and allocation overhead, not just the kernel. Expose an independent target-range kernel suitable for A's static partitions, and retain a reference path wherever numerical equivalence is unproved.",
      "C": "Research an alternative symmetry kernel that shares expensive reciprocal-distance calculations without reordering force sums. Use O(n) force accumulators and a serial lexicographic upper-triangle traversal: for each i, retain its accumulated lower-index contributions, evaluate its self interaction, then process j greater than i in ascending order, updating both directed accumulators. This preserves each body's original source order provided lower and upper portions are not separately reduced and recombined. Compute each directed displacement and multiply-accumulate with reference semantics; do not merely negate an already rounded forward force. Share inv_dist and inv_dist3 only after establishing identical squared-distance arithmetic in both directions. Check eligibility each iteration and use the original kernel for non-finite positions or other unproved cases. Preserve self interactions. Measure whether reducing reciprocal-distance evaluations toward n(n+1)/2 outweighs extra accumulator traffic. Treat this as a standalone alternative: naive parallel pair updates introduce races and reordered sums.",
      "G": "Integrate only complete candidates accompanied by correctness results and measurements from the unchanged harness. Establish the fastest validated standalone program first, then prioritize combining A's persistent target partitioning with B's independent target-lane SIMD kernel. Preserve both phase barriers, arithmetic semantics, tails and the binary interface. C's shared-accumulator traversal is not a drop-in parallel kernel; combine it only with a demonstrated ordering and race-freedom argument. Evaluate every actual integration end to end: layout conversions, register pressure, synchronization and startup can erase standalone gains. Never multiply standalone speedups or presume a merge wins. Within existing budgets, compare integrations against their strongest input and retain the fastest reproducible correct candidate, even if it is unmerged or the baseline. Do not alter tests, oracle, compiler configuration, resource limits or target, and do not dispatch on known test identities or expected answers.",
      "analysis": "All roles target Problem C, src/nbody.c, not the other contest problems. The only measured program is the valid baseline: mean 0.666653 seconds, samples 0.665785–0.668133 seconds, and four passing correctness cases. No optimized measurements, workload-size distribution or numerical tolerance are supplied. The source suggests the ten O(n²) force sweeps are the main opportunity on four ARM64 CPU cores with no GPU. Preserve the native integer input count followed by six-float body records, output records without a count, original body order, ten iterations, DT and SOFTENING. Forces must use unchanged positions for each iteration. Numerically, inv_dist is float(1.0 / sqrt((double)sqrd_dist)), not a float reciprocal square root. Preserve accumulation order, precision transitions and fixed-build contraction behavior; passing four cases alone does not establish correctness for every valid input. The portfolio separates multicore execution, exact SIMD/layout work and symmetry-based arithmetic reuse."
